/Alt (Four bar charts compare tendon-bone fixation properties at three angles \(ten degrees in blue, twenty degrees in orange, thirty degrees in green\) and various pretension levels from thirty to ninety newtons: Panel A shows mean contact pressure rising with pretension, highest at twenty degrees; Panel B shows consistently higher active contact area at ten and thirty degrees; Panel C presents mean relative displacement increasing with pretension, peaking at twenty degrees; Panel D displays peak tendon-side von Mises stress, highest at thirty degrees and increasing with pretension.)
/K [0 870 0 R]
/P 121 0 R
/Pg 41 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (FIGURE 6)
/Type /StructElem
>>
